WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.328
[...]

00:00:04.328 --> 00:00:07.206
In some societies,
members of groups that

00:00:07.206 --> 00:00:11.205
have suffered discrimination, or
social and economic disadvantage,

00:00:11.205 --> 00:00:14.200
are given special
consideration when they

00:00:14.200 --> 00:00:17.543
apply for jobs or university admission.

00:00:17.543 --> 00:00:20.868
Some people favor such
policies on the grounds

00:00:20.868 --> 00:00:24.733
that they can help bring
about a more equal society.

00:00:24.733 --> 00:00:28.191
Others oppose such
policies on the grounds

00:00:28.191 --> 00:00:32.163
that they are an unjust form
of reverse discrimination.

00:00:32.163 --> 00:00:33.572
What do you think?

00:00:33.572 --> 00:00:38.860
Is it just or unjust to give
preference to applicants

00:00:38.860 --> 00:00:42.820
who are members of groups that
have been discriminated against?

